	# ---- Nutaku F2P story: chapters, goals, rival bids. {n} = the goal's need, {target}/{hours} = the bid's; filled by f2p_ui.gd
	"f2p_ch_c1_title": "One derelict floor",
	"f2p_ch_c1_intro": "The same week, you are fired and evicted. What's left fits in one box and one envelope: the deed to one derelict floor of Harbour Street that nobody else wanted. Castellan Voss owns the rest of the street. He watches you carry the box in and laughs loud enough to be heard across it. Mirei, who managed his buildings for twelve years until his letter last Friday, is sitting on your step. 'I know where the fuse box is,' she says. 'It's all I've got.'",
	"f2p_ch_c1_g0": "Open {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c1_g1": "Get one floor to a {n}-link chain",
	"f2p_ch_c1_g2": "Earn {n} affection tiers with anyone",
	"f2p_ch_c1_outro": "Three floors lit on a dark street. Voss stops laughing. The next morning a city inspector's car is parked outside, and Voss is at his window, smiling again.",
	"f2p_ch_c2_title": "The fire inspection",
	"f2p_ch_c2_intro": "Voss reported you. Inspector Kaminski arrives with a clipboard and no expression: 'Every floor full enough to be supervised, and nobody on it working next to a man who talks through their headphones.' Then Voss buys the bank's loan on your floors, and calls it in.",
	"f2p_ch_c2_g0": "Open all {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c2_g1": "Pass inspection: every floor holds {n}+ pieces and no floor pays Wes's tax",
	"f2p_ch_c2_g2": "Repay Voss's loan in time",
	"f2p_ch_c2_boss_title": "Voss calls in the loan",
	"f2p_ch_c2_boss_text": "Voss owns your loan now and wants it repaid in full: {target}, due in {hours} hours. Earn it from the building before he can take it.",
	"f2p_ch_c2_outro": "Kaminski signs the certificate. You pay Voss to the last coin, and he has to count it himself. Across town the Glass Tower has gone half-empty, and its lender, Pike Harlan Capital, is looking for a buyer it can bully.",
	"f2p_ch_c3_title": "Glass and debt",
	"f2p_ch_c3_intro": "The Glass Tower is beautiful, half-empty and in debt to Pike Harlan Capital. You sell Harbour Street to the tenants who helped you fill it and buy the tower. Ms. Arden of Pike Harlan visits with a tablet and a smile: 'We'd simply like to be kept informed.' Everyone can see into every floor, which means everyone can see which floors are empty.",
	"f2p_ch_c3_g0": "Open {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c3_g1": "{n} fit-out levels across the tower",
	"f2p_ch_c3_g2": "{n} staff on the roster",
	"f2p_ch_c3_outro": "The floors fill, and Arden's tablet shows your numbers going up. She stops smiling, which is the first honest thing she has done. That night the night staff hold a meeting without you.",
	"f2p_ch_c4_title": "The strike",
	"f2p_ch_c4_intro": "At midnight the night staff walk out, together and politely: better chairs, better coffee, and someone who listens. They're right, and you were busy. Pike Harlan calls the strike 'a default event' and starts drafting a bid for your tower.",
	"f2p_ch_c4_g0": "Fit out every floor to level {n} (better chairs)",
	"f2p_ch_c4_g1": "Finish {n} staff requests (someone who listens)",
	"f2p_ch_c4_g2": "Open all {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c4_g3": "Beat Pike Harlan's bid",
	"f2p_ch_c4_boss_title": "Pike Harlan's bid",
	"f2p_ch_c4_boss_text": "Arden files a bid for the tower's debt: {target}, due in {hours} hours unless the building makes it first. Make it first.",
	"f2p_ch_c4_outro": "The staff come back on a Tuesday with cake. Pike's bid expires unanswered. And Voss, who has been quiet for a month, buys every building on the night market lane but one.",
	"f2p_ch_c5_title": "Lanterns",
	"f2p_ch_c5_intro": "Night Market Lofts: paper lanterns, noodle steam, and a Voss & Daughters sign going up on every building on the lane but this one. The council wrote the lane's old traders off years ago. They'd like to see what you do.",
	"f2p_ch_c5_g0": "Open {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c5_g1": "{n} affection tiers in total",
	"f2p_ch_c5_g2": "Get one floor to a {n}-link chain",
	"f2p_ch_c5_outro": "The lane votes on where to hold the lantern festival. It is not the building with Voss's sign on it. Voss files a complaint the same evening.",
	"f2p_ch_c6_title": "The noise complaint",
	"f2p_ch_c6_intro": "The complaint is about noise, filed by a tenant who turns out to work for Voss. Kaminski is back, apologetic: 'Rules are rules. Quiet floors, full floors, or I close you for the festival.' Then Voss bids for the whole lane.",
	"f2p_ch_c6_g0": "Open all {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c6_g1": "No floor pays Wes's tax (quiet floors)",
	"f2p_ch_c6_g2": "Every floor holds {n}+ pieces",
	"f2p_ch_c6_g3": "Win the bidding war for the lane",
	"f2p_ch_c6_boss_title": "The bidding war",
	"f2p_ch_c6_boss_text": "Voss bids for the whole lane, Lofts included: {target}. The lane's owners give you {hours} hours to match it from the building's own earnings.",
	"f2p_ch_c6_outro": "The festival goes ahead. Voss attends in a very good suit and buys a lantern from Priya without making eye contact. On the way out he mentions, to nobody in particular, that Pike Harlan is buying the Meridian's debt.",
	"f2p_ch_c7_title": "The Meridian",
	"f2p_ch_c7_intro": "The Meridian is a real office tower: lobbies, lifts, a fountain nobody turns off. You buy it the week Pike Harlan points its boardroom window at yours from next door. Nia used to audit Pike's books. She asks for the corner office and a very good pencil.",
	"f2p_ch_c7_g0": "Open {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c7_g1": "Staff ranks adding up to {n}",
	"f2p_ch_c7_g2": "{n} fit-out levels across the building",
	"f2p_ch_c7_outro": "Arden sends a fruit basket with no card. Mara scans it for bugs anyway. There are two. The next morning Pike Harlan starts buying your debt on the open market.",
	"f2p_ch_c8_title": "Hostile takeover",
	"f2p_ch_c8_intro": "Pike Harlan is buying the Meridian's debt to take the building. To fight a takeover it has to look like a building worth keeping, so Nia runs the audit her old firm wouldn't let her finish: every floor up to standard before the fund moves.",
	"f2p_ch_c8_g0": "Open all {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c8_g1": "The audit: every floor fitted out to level {n}",
	"f2p_ch_c8_g2": "Beat the hostile takeover",
	"f2p_ch_c8_boss_title": "The takeover",
	"f2p_ch_c8_boss_text": "The fund tables its offer: {target} for the Meridian's debt. Out-earn it in {hours} hours and the board will not sell.",
	"f2p_ch_c8_outro": "The board declines Pike Harlan's offer, seven votes to none. Arden sends you her resignation from Pike, with a CV. And across the harbour, Voss unveils the tallest tower on the skyline, with his name on the top floor.",
	"f2p_ch_c9_title": "Occupancy One",
	"f2p_ch_c9_intro": "Occupancy One stands one street over from Voss's tower, and nine floors higher. Nobody could fill it; the last owner wrote it off. Voss owns the ground lease under it and has never let anyone build above the lobby. You buy it anyway.",
	"f2p_ch_c9_g0": "Open {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c9_g1": "{n} affection tiers in total",
	"f2p_ch_c9_g2": "Take {n} an hour",
	"f2p_ch_c9_outro": "The tower's windows light up floor by floor, and the whole city can see it. So can Voss, from a lower window than he's used to. He calls Pike Harlan.",
	"f2p_ch_c10_title": "Keys to the city",
	"f2p_ch_c10_intro": "The showdown. Voss, with Pike Harlan's money behind him, bids for the ground lease, the tower and everything under it: the biggest number anyone has said out loud on this street. If he wins, you're back where you started, with one box and one envelope.",
	"f2p_ch_c10_g0": "Open all {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c10_g1": "{n} affection tiers in total",
	"f2p_ch_c10_g2": "Beat Voss's last bid",
	"f2p_ch_c10_boss_title": "Voss's last bid",
	"f2p_ch_c10_boss_text": "{target}, from Voss with Pike Harlan's money, due in {hours} hours. The tower has to out-earn its own price.",
	"f2p_ch_c10_outro": "Voss's bid fails. He crosses the street for the first time in twenty years, shakes Mirei's hand, then yours, and asks whether the top floor is taken. It is. Everyone you hired when nobody else would is up there, his tower looks small from the window, and the night is warm.",
