	"f2p_ev_uev_u1_text": "Arden is learning which floors creak.",
	"f2p_bn_bn_u1_title": "Clean Slate",
	"who_arden": "Arden",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_1_title": "Arden's new desk",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_1_text": "Arden moves into the Exchange's old clerk's office and puts one thing on the desk: a plant, still in the pot from the shop. 'It's staying,' she says.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_2_title": "The Calder Gazette",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_2_text": "Port Calder's paper runs a small item: 'Old Exchange sold to out-of-town landlord.' Sol reads it and says the headline could be better. She sends them one.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_3_title": "Crane's lunch",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_3_text": "Crane books the table next to Mirei's at lunch, every day this week, and never says a word. Mirei orders dessert every day, to make him wait.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_4_title": "The opening bell",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_4_text": "Someone has polished the Exchange's old bell. Nobody admits to it. Priya has brass polish on her sleeve.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_5_title": "A vote is called",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u1_5_text": "The planning board puts the Exchange on its agenda for next month. Councillor Hale's name is at the top of the list.",
	"f2p_pk_u2_title": "Closing Bell",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u2_title": "Survey Week",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u2_text": "Rafe is surveying every floor with a torch and a notebook.",
	"f2p_bn_bn_u2_title": "Hard Hat",
	"who_rafe": "Rafe",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_1_title": "Survey notes",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_1_text": "Rafe's survey notebook is full by Wednesday. The last page just says 'good building' and is underlined twice.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_2_title": "The stadium model",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_2_text": "Hale unveils a model of his stadium in the town hall lobby. The Exchange is not in it. Arden photographs it for the file.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_3_title": "Scaffold lunch",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_3_text": "The staff start eating lunch on Rafe's scaffold. Rafe puts up a sign about weight limits and then sits under it.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_4_title": "A letter from the council",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_4_text": "The council writes to say the Exchange is 'under review.' Nia writes back asking which clause. Nobody answers.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_5_title": "Postmark: Saint Aubin",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u2_5_text": "A postcard arrives from the coast with a picture of a grand hotel and no message. Mirei pins it above her desk anyway.",
	"f2p_pk_u3_title": "Saint Aubin",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u3_title": "Grand Reopening",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u3_text": "The Marlowe's doors are open again, and Juno is on the door.",
	"f2p_bn_bn_u3_title": "Suite 1204",
	"who_juno": "Juno",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_1_title": "Juno's first morning",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_1_text": "Juno is at the Marlowe's front desk at six, in gloves, learning the booking system from the night porter. She takes notes.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_2_title": "The seafront",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_2_text": "Every other hotel on the Saint Aubin seafront has a Lisle flag on the roof. The Marlowe puts up a plain white one. It looks better.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_3_title": "Lisle's inspector",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_3_text": "A man from Lisle Hotels books a room, checks every tap and leaves a one-star review. The review praises the bar.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_4_title": "The ballroom",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_4_text": "Mara unlocks the Marlowe's ballroom for the first time since 2003. There is a piano in it, under a sheet. Nobody knows whose it is.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_5_title": "A name on a card",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u3_5_text": "The name Lisle left behind, Cordelia Thorne, turns out to own forty empty apartments on the coast. Arden starts a file.",
	"f2p_pk_u4_title": "Last Call",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u4_title": "Jazz Week",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u4_text": "Lark is playing two sets a night, and taking requests.",
	"f2p_bn_bn_u4_title": "Midnight Set",
	"who_lark": "Lark",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_1_title": "Lark's rehearsal",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_1_text": "Lark rehearses in the empty ballroom at noon. The kitchen staff stop working to listen, and nobody tells them to start again.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_2_title": "The fire escapes",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_2_text": "Priya spends a whole day with a grinder freeing the Marlowe's fire escapes. The last bolt comes out at sunset. Everybody claps.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_3_title": "Thorne's viewing",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_3_text": "Cordelia Thorne tours the Marlowe with three assistants and says 'lovely bones' eleven times. Juno counts.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_4_title": "The recording light",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_4_text": "A red 'recording' light goes up outside the ballroom. Guests walk past it on tiptoe for a week.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_5_title": "A letter from Northgate",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u4_5_text": "A letter from Northgate, addressed to 'whoever beat Pike Harlan,' asks for a meeting. It is signed O. Brandt.",
	"f2p_pk_u5_title": "Northgate",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u5_title": "Stakeout",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u5_text": "Opal is watching Rook's shell companies from the last arch.",
	"f2p_bn_bn_u5_title": "Cold Case",
	"who_odile": "Opal",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_1_title": "The last arch",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_1_text": "Opal's office in the last arch has a kettle, a filing cabinet and a camp bed. 'The bed is for thinking,' she says.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_2_title": "Market night",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_2_text": "The Northgate night market opens in the arches you own, and the stall rents go down, not up. The traders notice.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_3_title": "Rook's men",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_3_text": "Two of Rook's men come to measure the arches. Mara asks for their paperwork, and they leave to find some.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_4_title": "The ledger",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_4_text": "Nia takes a train north to read Rook's filings with Opal. They find the same accountant's signature on all three shell companies.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_5_title": "A trust in the post",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u5_5_text": "A letter arrives from a trust nobody has heard of, offering to buy the arches 'at a fair valuation.' It is signed Penhale.",
	"f2p_pk_u6_title": "The Deed",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u6_title": "Open Archive",
	"f2p_ev_uev_u6_text": "Teo is keeping the archive open late, for anyone who asks.",
	"f2p_bn_bn_u6_title": "First Edition",
	"who_teo": "Teo",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_1_title": "The archive",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_1_text": "Teo shows you the Northgate archive: nine rooms, one kettle, and every deed the city has signed since 1850.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_2_title": "The 1904 drawer",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_2_text": "Teo finds the drawer marked 1904 stuck shut. Rafe takes it apart with a screwdriver in four minutes.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_3_title": "The traders' meeting",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_3_text": "The market traders hold a meeting in the biggest arch. Two hundred people come. Opal counts them twice.",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_4_title": "Sol's photographer",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_4_text": "Sol sends her photographer north with instructions to 'stand near the courthouse and look bored.'",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_5_title": "The whole family",
	"f2p_dp_dp_u6_5_text": "Mirei takes the night train north with the whole staff, from Harbour Street on. Voss sees them off at the station and says nothing, but he waves.",
	"f2p_bld_6": "The Exchange",
	"f2p_bld_7": "Hotel Marlowe",
	"f2p_bld_8": "The Viaduct Arches",
	"f2p_sc_ot_c10_hearing": "The courthouse steps",
	"f2p_sc_ot_arden_1": "Hair down",
	"f2p_sc_ot_arden_2": "The last pearl",
	"f2p_sc_ot_b6": "The trading floor",
	"f2p_sc_ot_rafe_1": "Scaffold at sunset",
	"f2p_sc_ot_rafe_2": "Load-bearing",
	"f2p_sc_ot_juno_1": "Suite 1204",
	"f2p_sc_ot_juno_2": "Sunrise on the balcony",
	"f2p_sc_ot_b7": "The Marlowe bar",
	"f2p_sc_ot_lark_1": "After hours",
	"f2p_sc_ot_lark_2": "The midnight song",
	"f2p_sc_ot_odile_1": "Almost closed",
	"f2p_sc_ot_odile_2": "Off duty",
	"f2p_sc_ot_b8": "Under the arches",
	"f2p_sc_ot_teo_1": "The reading room",
	"f2p_sc_ot_teo_2": "First light",
	"f2p_tier_arden_1": "The day of the Meridian vote, Pike wrote me off. I resigned before they could say it out loud. Four years I took buildings apart. Show me how you keep one standing.",
	"f2p_tier_arden_2": "You gave me every lease in the Exchange. Nobody's ever handed me something to keep. At Pike I ate lunch at my desk for four years. Today I'd rather eat it on the roof. With you.",
	"f2p_tier_arden_4": "Crane offered me twice my Pike salary to help him write this building off. I told him I'd already been promoted. By myself. It felt wonderful.",
	"f2p_tier_rafe_1": "This ceiling has been holding itself up out of spite since 1931. I respect that. I'd like to help.",
	"f2p_tier_rafe_2": "You asked what the cracks mean. Nobody asks. Most people want me to say 'fine' and leave. Sit down, this takes a while.",
	"f2p_tier_rafe_4": "I signed off the ceiling today. Took me eleven weeks. I kept finding reasons to come back. You were most of them.",
	"f2p_tier_juno_1": "My father left the Marlowe to rot, and me with it. 'Sentimental,' he said, about both of us. I've decided that was his opinion, not mine.",
	"f2p_tier_juno_2": "Everyone in Saint Aubin calls me Miss Voss and waits for me to fail. You call me Juno and ask what I think. Do that again.",
	"f2p_tier_juno_4": "The Marlowe was full last night. Every room. I stood in the lobby at midnight and didn't know what to do with my hands. My father rang to congratulate me. I'll call him back tomorrow. Probably.",
	"f2p_tier_lark_1": "I had one hit, in 2004. The label dropped me a year later and said I was a one-song pianist. I play the same song at midnight every night. Nobody's ever asked what it's called.",
	"f2p_tier_lark_2": "Nine years, three owners, one piano. You're the first owner who stayed for the last set. I played something new tonight. First new song in years. Did you notice?",
	"f2p_tier_lark_4": "I've booked the ballroom. I'm recording an album in it: eleven new songs. The midnight one has a name now. I'm not telling you. You'll hear it.",
	"f2p_tier_odile_1": "Twelve years in the Northgate precinct. I reported my captain for taking Rook's money, and they retired me for it. I kept the coat, and one case I couldn't close.",
	"f2p_tier_odile_2": "Most people who talk to a detective want something found. You asked how my day was. I had to think about it. It was good, it turns out. It's been good for a while.",
	"f2p_tier_odile_4": "I put my name on the door of the last arch this morning. 'O. Brandt, Investigations.' Brass. It's crooked. I'm leaving it crooked. Also, I ran a background check on you the first week. It came back boring. I've never been so glad to be bored.",
	"f2p_tier_teo_1": "People think archives are quiet. They aren't. Every drawer is somebody arguing with somebody who died a hundred years ago.",
	"f2p_tier_teo_2": "You came down to the basement twice. Nobody comes down here twice. I've put the kettle on permanently.",
	"f2p_tier_teo_4": "I've read every deed in this city. I never once wanted to be in one of the stories. I'd like to be in yours.",
	"f2p_bt_c9_lobby_title": "The lobby lights",
	"f2p_bt_c9_lobby_text": "Priya rewires the tower's lobby so every light in it comes on at once. It takes her two nights and one argument with the fuse box, which she wins. From across the harbour the whole tower seems to wake up.",
	"f2p_bt_c10_hearing_title": "The ground-lease hearing",
	"f2p_bt_c10_hearing_text": "Voss's lawyers ask the court to freeze the tower's leases until the bid is settled. Kaminski is called as a witness and says the building is safe, which she points out is the only thing she has ever testified about.",
	"f2p_bt_c10_hearing_goal": "The hearing: every floor fitted out to level {n}",
	"f2p_bt_c10_steps_title": "The courthouse steps",
	"f2p_bt_c10_steps_text": "Mirei comes out of the courthouse at golden hour with the ruling in a folder, and doesn't open it until you're beside her. 'We keep the leases,' she says. 'For now.'",
	"f2p_bt_c10_voss_title": "Voss's envelope",
	"f2p_bt_c10_voss_text": "Voss comes to the tower's lobby with an envelope: your old job back, at twice the salary, if you walk away today. You read it twice. Mirei reads it once and laughs so hard the doorman comes over to check on her.",
	"f2p_bt_c10_arden_title": "A call from a payphone",
	"f2p_bt_c10_arden_text": "Arden calls from a payphone, which nobody uses any more. Voss and Pike Harlan have agreed the terms of the last bid, and she has a copy. She would like to bring it over, if the offer of a desk still stands.",
	"f2p_ch_c11_title": "Open outcry",
	"f2p_ch_c11_intro": "Port Calder, across the bay: a city of banks, and a stock exchange nobody has shouted a price in since the markets went electronic. Halloran Crane bought it to write off and knock down. He'll sell it to you, he says, because it's worth nothing. Arden reads the contract twice and says it's worth everything.",
	"f2p_ch_c11_outro": "The first tenants move onto the trading floor. Someone rings the old opening bell as a joke, and the whole building stops to listen. Crane hears it from his office across the square, and calls the planning board.",
	"f2p_ch_c11_g0": "Open {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c11_g1": "Get one floor to a {n}-link chain",
	"f2p_ch_c11_g2": "Finish {n} staff requests",
	"f2p_bt_c11_letter_title": "Crane's letter",
	"f2p_bt_c11_letter_text": "A letter arrives on Crane's paper, addressed to Arden: a car, a corner office and her old salary twice over, if she walks. She reads it once, feeds it to the shredder, and asks whether the shredder can be expensed.",
	"f2p_ch_c12_title": "Closing bell",
	"f2p_ch_c12_intro": "Councillor Edmund Hale wants the Exchange's block for his stadium. His city engineer shuts the trading floor until the ceiling is certified ('eighty tonnes of historic plaster'), and while the hall is closed Hale tables a compulsory purchase. Rafe Okonkwo, the one engineer in Port Calder who'll sign against the council, turns up with a torch.",
	"f2p_ch_c12_outro": "The purchase fails at the board, four votes to three. The ceiling holds, as Rafe said it would. And a postcard arrives from Saint Aubin, on the coast, signed Juno Voss: 'My father wrote me off. I'd like to sell you his hotel.'",
	"f2p_ch_c12_g0": "Open all {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c12_g1": "Certify the ceiling: every floor fitted out to level {n}",
	"f2p_ch_c12_g2": "Beat the compulsory purchase",
	"f2p_ch_c12_boss_title": "The compulsory purchase",
	"f2p_ch_c12_boss_text": "Hale values the Exchange at {target} and moves to buy it for the city. Out-earn his valuation in {hours} hours and the board can't justify it.",
	"f2p_bt_c12_survey_title": "The ceiling survey",
	"f2p_bt_c12_survey_text": "Rafe climbs into the roof space with a torch and comes down grinning and grey with dust. 'Good news,' he says. 'It's only mostly held up by spite.'",
	"f2p_ch_c13_title": "Room service",
	"f2p_ch_c13_intro": "Saint Aubin, on the coast. The Hotel Marlowe was the grandest hotel on the seafront until Castellan Voss wrote it off and handed it to the daughter he'd written off too. Juno Voss sells it to you for a fair price and one promise: the bar stays open. Augustin Lisle, who owns every other hotel on the front, sends a very large bouquet and a very small offer.",
	"f2p_ch_c13_outro": "The Marlowe's bar fills for the first time in years. Lisle sits in the far booth, orders a drink he doesn't touch, and leaves a card on the table with someone else's name on it: Cordelia Thorne.",
	"f2p_ch_c13_g0": "Open {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c13_g1": "Get one floor to a {n}-link chain",
	"f2p_ch_c13_g2": "{n} fit-out levels across the hotel",
	"f2p_bt_c13_booth_title": "The far booth",
	"f2p_bt_c13_booth_text": "Augustin Lisle takes the far booth in the Marlowe's bar every night that week, alone, and never orders. On the fifth night he leaves a note for Juno. It says: 'The fire escapes.'",
	"f2p_ch_c14_title": "Last call",
	"f2p_ch_c14_intro": "Lisle's note was right. The Marlowe's fire escapes were painted over in 1987 and bolted shut in 1992, and the coast's inspector gives you a week. The same morning Cordelia Thorne, who turns grand hotels into empty short-lets, bids for the Marlowe with Lisle's money. Juno takes it personally.",
	"f2p_ch_c14_outro": "Thorne's bid fails. Juno's father sends flowers with a card in his own handwriting. Lark plays the album's first song to a full bar. And a letter arrives from Northgate, a railway city in the north, from a detective nobody believed.",
	"f2p_ch_c14_g0": "Open all {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c14_g1": "Fire escapes: every floor holds {n}+ pieces and no floor pays Wes's tax",
	"f2p_ch_c14_g2": "Beat Cordelia Thorne's bid",
	"f2p_ch_c14_boss_title": "Thorne's bid",
	"f2p_ch_c14_boss_text": "Cordelia Thorne bids {target} for the Marlowe, cash, sight unseen. Juno asks you to make it clear, within {hours} hours, that the hotel isn't for sale.",
	"f2p_bt_c14_drill_title": "The fire drill",
	"f2p_bt_c14_drill_text": "The inspector runs the drill at four in the afternoon. Every guest is on the promenade in ninety seconds, including Cordelia Thorne, who happened to be in the lobby, and who times it on her own watch.",
	"f2p_ch_c15_title": "Shell game",
	"f2p_ch_c15_intro": "Northgate: nine brick arches under the old railway, a night market in each, and a landlord, Silas Rook, who lets them rot around the traders. Opal Brandt keeps an office in the last arch and a wall of string that ends at Rook. 'Three shell companies,' she says. 'All buying the arches. All him.'",
	"f2p_ch_c15_outro": "Opal pins the last photograph to the wall and steps back. The string runs past Rook, to a trust with offices in every city you've built in, and a spokesman called Penhale.",
	"f2p_ch_c15_g0": "Open {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c15_g1": "Every arch pays its way: {n} fit-out levels across the arches",
	"f2p_ch_c15_g2": "Finish {n} staff requests",
	"f2p_bt_c15_wall_title": "The wall of string",
	"f2p_bt_c15_wall_text": "Opal shows you the wall at midnight, by torchlight, like a magic trick. Every arch you've bought is on it. So is a trust you've never heard of, which has been buying Rook's debts for a year.",
	"f2p_ch_c16_title": "The deed",
	"f2p_ch_c16_intro": "Teo Marsh, Northgate's archivist, finds it in a drawer marked 1904: the deed that gave the arches to the market traders for as long as the arches are full. The Sterling Trust, which bought Rook's debts, hears the same afternoon, and bids for everything under the railway before the arches can fill.",
	"f2p_ch_c16_outro": "The Trust's bid fails in public, on the courthouse steps, in front of Sol's photographer. The traders keep their arches, and Opal closes her case. On the roof of the last arch everyone who helped, from Harbour Street to here, is waiting, and the night is warm. Somewhere, Mr. Penhale is making a phone call.",
	"f2p_ch_c16_g0": "Open all {n} floors",
	"f2p_ch_c16_g1": "Every floor fitted out to level {n}",
	"f2p_ch_c16_g2": "Beat the Trust's bid",
	"f2p_ch_c16_boss_title": "The Trust's bid",
	"f2p_ch_c16_boss_text": "{target} for every arch in Northgate, from the Sterling Trust. Mr. Penhale gives the city {hours} hours to decide. Give it a better answer.",
	"f2p_bt_c16_clause_title": "The 1904 clause",
	"f2p_bt_c16_clause_text": "Teo reads the 1904 clause aloud in the archive, twice, then a third time down the phone to Mirei. The arches belong to whoever keeps them full. Mirei is quiet for a long time. Then she asks how many are empty.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_1_title": "The night porter's chair",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_1_l0": "There's a chair in the lobby nobody sits in. The night porter's. He retired in 2009 and Voss never replaced him.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_1_l1": "Why keep the chair?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_1_l2": "Because on the nights I couldn't sleep, I sat in it and watched the door. Tonight I thought I might let you have it. Just for an hour.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_2_title": "Two coffees",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_2_l0": "You take it black. I noticed on the second day. I didn't mean to. It's the sort of thing I file away.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_2_l1": "What else is in the file?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_2_l2": "That you say thank you to the lift. That you read the fire notices. That I've started buying two coffees without deciding to.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_3_title": "What the building is for",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_3_l0": "My mother ran a boarding house on this street. Twelve rooms. Voss bought it in 1998 and knocked it through into offices. I managed the building that swallowed hers for twelve years.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_3_l1": "Why did you stay?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mirei_3_l2": "Because I was good at it and nobody else would have me. Then you walked in with one box and a deed. Now I'm good at it for us. She'd have liked you.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_1_title": "The fourth-floor machine",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_1_l0": "I've mapped every coffee machine in the building. The one on four has a personality. It's not a good personality.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_1_l1": "And yet you keep using it.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_1_l2": "Loyalty. Also it's the closest. Mostly it's the closest. Don't tell it I said that.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_2_title": "Rollback",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_2_l0": "I broke production once. Twelve years ago. Took down a bank's website for forty minutes. I still dream about it.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_2_l1": "What happened after?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_2_l2": "My manager bought me a sandwich and said, 'Now you'll never do it again.' He was right. I've been trying to be that guy ever since.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_3_title": "The second shirt",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_3_l0": "People think I wear the same shirt every day. I own four identical shirts. It's a system.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_3_l1": "A system for what?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_dan_3_l2": "For never having to decide anything before coffee. You're the first thing in years I've wanted to decide about.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_1_title": "The good ledge",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_1_l0": "Every roof has a good ledge. Out of the wind, facing west, warm from the afternoon. You have to find it with your hands.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_1_l1": "Did you find this one's?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_1_l2": "First day. I haven't told facilities. I'm telling you, which means I trust you, which means don't sit on it without me.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_2_title": "Wiring diagram",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_2_l0": "Whoever wired the third floor in 1974 was either a genius or drunk. The labels are poems. 'Hall. Not that hall. The other hall.'",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_2_l1": "Can you fix it?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_2_l2": "I can fix anything. I just want to keep one of the labels first. Frame it. Hang it in the lift. Someone should see it.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_3_title": "Hard hat",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_3_l0": "My dad was an electrician. He gave me his hard hat when I qualified. It's two sizes too big. I wear it anyway.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_3_l1": "Does he know you're up on roofs at sunset?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_priya_3_l2": "He knows. He told me to bring someone who holds the ladder without being asked. I told him I had.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_1_title": "The key ring",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_1_l0": "Two hundred and eleven keys. I know every one by feel. I can open the boiler room in the dark.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_1_l1": "Have you ever had to?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_1_l2": "Twice. Both times it was Wes. Both times he said he was 'looking for a quiet place to think.' I have thoughts about that.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_2_title": "Drill schedule",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_2_l0": "Fire drills are the only time everyone in the building stands in one place. I like counting them. Everyone's there. Everyone's fine.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_2_l1": "That's the best part of your job?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_2_l2": "That's the best part of my week. Don't make that face. It's a nice feeling. Knowing where everyone is.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_3_title": "The scar",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_3_l0": "You've been not-asking about the eyebrow for weeks. It's a filing cabinet. 2016. It lost.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_3_l1": "The cabinet lost?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_mara_3_l2": "I had it taken out of the building. Nothing in here gets to hurt anyone twice. That includes furniture. It includes me.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_1_title": "The pitch",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_1_l0": "Give me thirty seconds and I can sell you anything. A pen. A building. A second opinion.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_1_l1": "Sell me the couch on seven.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_1_l2": "I can't. It's the only thing I've ever wanted to keep. That's never happened before. I'm a bit unsettled, honestly.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_2_title": "Headphones",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_2_l0": "Everyone wears headphones when I'm near. I noticed. I'm not stupid, just loud.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_2_l1": "You could talk less.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_2_l2": "I've tried. It turns out I only talk this much when I'm nervous. I'm nervous around you, which is new. So. Sorry in advance.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_3_title": "Nia's audit",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_3_l0": "Nia audited my expenses. She found a receipt for a book I bought you and flagged it 'personal, allowed.'",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_3_l1": "That's kind of her.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_wes_3_l2": "It's the kindest thing an auditor has ever written about me. I'm having it framed. Next to the couch.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_1_title": "Reconciled",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_1_l0": "Most people's numbers are a story they tell themselves. Yours are just numbers. It's very restful.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_1_l1": "Is that a compliment?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_1_l2": "It's the highest one I have. I've used it twice in my career. The other one was a spreadsheet.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_2_title": "Pencil",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_2_l0": "I keep a pencil behind my ear because pens are permanent and I'm not, most days, sure yet.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_2_l1": "About what?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_2_l2": "About anything. Lately I've been sure about one or two things. I might have to switch to ink. It's alarming.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_3_title": "Day off",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_3_l0": "I've never taken a day off in six years. HR sends me a letter about it every March.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_3_l1": "Take one. Take tomorrow.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_nia_3_l2": "Only if you do too. I'm not spending my first day off learning what people do on days off without a second opinion.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_1_title": "Four o'clock",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_1_l0": "The paper folded eight years ago. I still file a column at four o'clock every day. It goes in a drawer.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_1_l1": "Can I read the drawer?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_1_l2": "Nobody's asked that. There are two thousand columns in it. Start with March 2019. That was a good month for sentences.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_2_title": "Correction",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_2_l0": "Voss wrote to ask for a correction. I'd described his suit as 'expensive.' He wants 'very expensive.'",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_2_l1": "Will you print it?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_2_l2": "I'll print it. Page one. Nobody has ever asked me for a correction that made them look worse. I'm almost fond of him.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_3_title": "The headline",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_3_l0": "I write a headline for every day before it happens. Most are wrong. It's good practice for being surprised.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_3_l1": "What was today's?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_sol_3_l2": "'Local woman stays late for no reason.' It was wrong. There was a reason. You were sitting right there.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_1_title": "The tablet",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_1_l0": "I carried this tablet for four years at Pike. Every building on it was something I was supposed to take.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_1_l1": "What's on it now?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_1_l2": "Floor plans. Birthdays. Which tenant likes the window seat. It's the same tablet. It's a much better list.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_2_title": "Ms. Arden",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_2_l0": "At Pike nobody used my first name in four years. I wasn't sure I still had one.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_2_l1": "Imogen.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_2_l2": "Yes. That's it. That's the one. Say it at the coffee machine tomorrow, where people can hear. I'd like to get used to it.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_3_title": "Resignation",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_3_l0": "I wrote my resignation from Pike eleven times before I sent it. Every draft was politer than the last.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_3_l1": "What did the one you sent say?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_arden_3_l2": "'No.' Then my name. I've never enjoyed writing anything so much. I kept a copy. It's on the fridge.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_1_title": "Tap test",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_1_l0": "Knock on a wall and it tells you what's inside it. Hollow, solid, pipe, somebody's old sandwich.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_1_l1": "What does this wall say?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_1_l2": "It says it was built by people who were proud of it. You can hear that. Not many walls say it any more.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_2_title": "The third rung",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_2_l0": "The third rung on that scaffold is loose. I leave it loose on purpose.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_2_l1": "That seems dangerous.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_2_l2": "It makes everyone slow down on the way up. Best safety feature I ever built. Nobody slows down for a sign.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_3_title": "Sign-off",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_3_l0": "My signature on a certificate means a building won't fall on anybody. I've signed four hundred of them.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_3_l1": "Do you remember them all?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_rafe_3_l2": "Every one. This is the only one where I kept inventing reasons to come back and check it again.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_1_title": "The gloves",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_1_l0": "My father never takes his gloves off to shake hands. I started wearing them at twenty to annoy him. Now I can't stop.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_1_l1": "Do you want to stop?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_1_l2": "Ask me again when I've shaken yours. Without them. I'm working up to it. You'll know when.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_2_title": "Room 1204",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_2_l0": "Every Voss hotel has one room the family keeps for itself. At the Marlowe it's 1204. I gave the key to the front desk.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_2_l1": "Why?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_2_l2": "Because a room nobody sleeps in is just a museum. Book it for someone who's having a bad week. Anyone. Not my father.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_3_title": "Dinner with Castellan",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_3_l0": "My father asked me to dinner. First time in three years. I said I'd bring someone.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_3_l1": "Me?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_juno_3_l2": "You. He'll be rude for the first course and charming by dessert. It's his only move. You'll be fine. I'll be under the table, kicking him.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_1_title": "Requests",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_1_l0": "People request the same six songs. I could play them asleep. Some nights I think I have.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_1_l1": "Play something nobody requests.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_1_l2": "Careful. Say that twice and I'll play for an hour. The bar will empty. I won't notice. You might have to carry me home.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_2_title": "The piano's name",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_2_l0": "This piano is called Gerald. It was named by a drunk trombonist in 1981 and it stuck.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_2_l1": "Gerald.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_2_l2": "Say it with respect. Gerald has outlived four owners and a flood. Gerald has opinions about the key of E flat.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_3_title": "Last set",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_3_l0": "The last set is for whoever's left. Usually it's the bartender and a man asleep in the corner.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_3_l1": "Tonight it's me.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_lark_3_l2": "Tonight it's you. I noticed. I played it slower. Don't tell the bartender; he likes to go home.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_1_title": "The wall",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_1_l0": "Every detective has a wall. Mine has been up for six years. The string's faded to pink.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_1_l1": "Why not take it down?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_1_l2": "Because the day I take it down I've either solved it or given up. I haven't decided which of those scares me more.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_2_title": "Stakeout",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_2_l0": "The secret to a stakeout is snacks and somebody who doesn't need to talk. Most people fail the second one.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_2_l1": "I can be quiet.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_2_l2": "You've been quiet for an hour. It's the best hour I've had in this car. Pass the pretzels.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_3_title": "The badge",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_3_l0": "I still carry my old badge. It doesn't mean anything any more. It's just heavy in the right place.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_3_l1": "What will you carry when the case is closed?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_odile_3_l2": "I was going to say nothing. I've been thinking lately that the answer might be a person. Don't make it weird.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_1_title": "The kettle",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_1_l0": "The archive has a rule: no liquids near the documents. The kettle is forty feet away. I've measured it.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_1_l1": "Exactly forty?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_1_l2": "Forty-one. I moved it a foot when you started visiting. You gesture when you talk. I didn't want to lose the 1904 map.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_2_title": "Handwriting",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_2_l0": "You can tell a lot from how people signed their names in 1900. Confidence. Hurry. Whether they were in love.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_2_l1": "How can you tell that?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_2_l2": "They take longer over the capitals. Your note yesterday. The T. You took a very long time over the T.",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_3_title": "Filed under",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_3_l0": "I've been trying to decide where to file you. Not 'Tenants.' Not 'Correspondence.'",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_3_l1": "What did you decide?",
	"f2p_ss_ss_teo_3_l2": "I made a new drawer. It doesn't have a label yet. I'm told that's a good sign in a drawer.",
	"f2p_ms_story1": "Read a staff story",
	"f2p_ms_crisis1": "Settle the tenant crisis",
	"f2p_ms_hard1": "Play the night floor",
	"f2p_ms_decor2": "Claim {n} floor goals",
	# ---- end of gen_i18n.py section
},
